UNA Watch kernel
----------------

The UNA Watch port was written from the hardware as UNA Watch Ltd's own
kernel drives it: its source (https://github.com/UNAWatch/una-kernel-public,
MIT licence, below) and the bootloader image published with it. Taken from
it are register values, timings and sequences, among them those of the
display (LS012B7DD06A), the haptics (DRV2625), the fuel gauge's cell model
(MAX17262), the charger (PCA9420), the eMMC (SDMMC) and the USB PHY; the
format of its .ota update files (tools/una/pack_ota.py makes the same files);
the analysis in docs/boards/unawatch/hardware.md, which cites its sources
file by file; and tools/una/SecurityKeys.pem, the update key every UNA
Watch's bootloader uses, copied unchanged. That key is published by UNA Watch
Ltd and is not a secret.

